  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "### **Release Notes - Version 2.2.0**  \n**Refactor Rate Limiting, Pipeline Configuration, and Code Cleanup**  \n\n---\n\n## **🚀 What's New in 2.2.0?**  \nThis release brings **significant optimizations, refactors, and modular improvements** to the system, focusing on **rate limiting, pipeline configuration, and overall code clarity**.  \n\n---\n\n## **🔧 Enhancements & Optimizations**  \n\n### **📌 Rate Limiting Enhancements**  \n- Introduced **periodic expiration** for stale user/command pairs in `_buckets` to prevent memory bloat.  \n- Optimized bucket management logic for improved **efficiency and responsiveness**.  \n\n### **📌 Dispatcher Refactor for DRY Compliance**  \n- Removed **redundant reflection** in `Dispatcher`.  \n- Introduced a **centralized registry (`RequestMetadata`)** that eagerly stores metadata, reducing computation overhead.  \n- Results in **faster command execution** and **better maintainability**.  \n\n### **📌 Pipeline Configuration Refactor**  \n- Separated `DispatcherOptions` into **modular options classes** for better responsibility segregation:  \n  - `LoggingOptions`  \n  - `TimeoutOptions`  \n  - `ResilienceOptions`  \n- Added **`AddXBehavior` extension methods** to simplify **Dependency Injection (DI)** registration of pipeline behaviors.  \n- Updated existing implementations to use the new structured approach, improving readability and flexibility.  \n\n### **📌 Additional Improvements**  \n- **Command Exemptions:**  \n  - Commands can now be **exempted from multiple pipelines**, improving execution control.  \n- **General Code Cleanup:**  \n  - Refactored several components for **better readability, maintainability, and performance**.  \n\n---\n\n## **📂 Breaking Changes?**  \n✅ **No major breaking changes**—this version maintains backward compatibility while introducing a **more modular, maintainable, and optimized architecture**.  \n\n---\n\n## **⏭️ What’s Next?**  \n- Further enhancements to **pipeline behaviors and command execution**.  \n- Additional improvements to **performance and memory efficiency**.",
  "repository": "",
